+
+### VictoriaLogs: read-only incident log investigations
+
+For journal, nginx and application-log evidence that is not available through metrics, add
+**VictoriaLogs** under **Connectors → Add**, then configure its HTTP(S) origin as
+`vl_url`. Configure `vl_auth_method` only when needed (`none`, `bearer_token`,
+`basic_auth` or `custom_header`); token and password settings are treated as secrets
+in the connector form. Select the resulting connector for the agent's skill to grant
+access; simply creating it does not bypass the per-incident tool allowlist.
+
+The separate read-only `victoria_logs` tool provides `query`, `hits`,
+`field_names`, `field_values` and `stats_query`. Supply explicit RFC3339
+`start`/`end` times (maximum six-hour range); `query` returns up to 50 log
+records by default, or 200 when requested, and caps the provider response at
+256 KiB. This connector does not replace VictoriaMetrics PromQL/MetricsQL or
+grant permission to change infrastructure. It connects directly to the
+configured origin (no environment proxy); use a trusted provider endpoint and
+a read-only credential.
